# `for (const value of list)` over an array in double storage is the loop that a counter would give, unrolled eight times: eight element loads.
# BODY-LABEL: steps by 8
# BODY-COUNT-8: Double b@{{*}} = Load(b@{{*}}Reads:indexedDoubleProperties
# BODY-NOT: Reads:indexedDoubleProperties
# BODY-LABEL: end of loop
# Its only branch is the test of the counter. Nothing is called, polled or read again: no iterator, no result object, no length, no storage.
# HOT-LABEL: steps by 8
# HOT-NOT: Branch(
# HOT-NOT: isLoopPoll
# HOT-NOT: ExitsSideways
# HOT-NOT: Reads:Butterfly_publicLength
# HOT: Branch(b@{{*}}, Terminal, {{*}}:Less)
# HOT-NOT: Branch(
# HOT-NOT: isLoopPoll
# HOT-NOT: ExitsSideways
# HOT-LABEL: end of loop
# Eight elements cost ten instructions on x86-64: eight additions from memory, the counter, the branch.
# X64: instructions: 10, patchpoints: 0, {{*}} steps by 8
# ARM64: instructions: 19, patchpoints: 0, {{*}} steps by 8
